Denise Allen}{
 [00:10:29\u8211\'9600:10:44]\line Yeah. And, you know, vision therapy has been around that long, but nobody knew about it. I didn't know about it until I went looking for answers as a, you know, 40-something-year-old because my eyes were bothering me more at that point.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:10:44\u8211\'9600:10:50]\line Well, I think there's still a real lack of understanding about vision therapy.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:10:50\u8211\'9600:10:52]\line Absolutely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:10:53\u8211\'9600:11:26]\line Yeah, it was something I had heard about again in our journey with autism ourselves. It's just one of many avenues that you explore when you're dealing with communication. And I remember hearing about\u8212\'97 we have a place, I'm in the Seattle area, and checking out, but that was all new, just the whole idea of doing vision therapy. Because again, it's so\u8212\'97 you just think about it, you just get eye exams and you get glasses. You don't think about this as something, another area, although it makes perfect sense once you start. looking at it a little more closely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:11:26\u8211\'9600:12:11]\line Right. Yeah. And I didn't start looking until my eye turn started to become really bad in my 40s. I started to get presbyopia like a lot of us do at that age, you know, can't see till you're, you know, have your hand clear out here. And so my eye turn just got worse.\line And, and I looked at natural vision improvement things. And I I started searching online and I just by accident, not by accident, right? Came across vision therapy, found out there was a doctor just down the street from me. And there were only 2 in the whole state of Utah at that point. And went in and had an exam and figured out that there was something we could do.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:12:11\u8211\'9600:12:29]\line Wow. Well, that's, I'm glad that you found that. What was it like then? I mean, what and how? Tell me about that experience. As you\u8212\'97 after you went through, started going through the therapy, did you experience like true depth perception for the first time, or, you know, things like that?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:12:29\u8211\'9600:12:31]\line Well, it wasn't quite that easy.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:12:31\u8211\'9600:12:32]\line It wasn't like\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:12:32\u8211\'9600:13:08]\line Yeah, no, fair. Um, it, it was, uh, about 2013. I started vision therapy Did a lot of sessions of therapy, and I just wasn't getting any resolution at all. I wasn't getting any progress. And my doctor said, you know, you can look at surgery. That could be what you might want to do in addition. And I didn't want to do surgery, so I stopped vision therapy, took my daughter in, found out that she was mini-me and that she needed vision therapy. Wow.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:13:09\u8211\'9600:13:09]\line Okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:13:10\u8211\'9600:13:11]\line Well, and I knew\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:13:11\u8211\'9600:13:13]\line It's really genetic, it sounds like.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:13:13\u8211\'9600:13:53]\line Yeah, it's hard to say. Yeah, it's hard to say. But I mean, I have 6 children. My youngest daughter was just like me. I knew she was like me because she had had an eye turn when she was 3, like I did.\line And I had taken her to the doctor and they put her in glasses. It was just, you know, the same process. And she was fine. She did fine in school. She didn't seem to struggle that much in other things.\line She didn't seem to be super clumsy. I had done other things with her when she was very young, like music and movement. I taught music and movement classes. And so there were things that maybe compensated better. I don't know.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:13:53\u8211\'9600:13:53]\line Right.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:13:53\u8211\'9600:14:29]\line And I didn't see her doing poorly in school or having any struggles. And I had this passion for sharing the whole thing, you know, because I knew it could help. It hadn't helped me yet, but I knew it could. And so I was reading this book called When Your Sorry, When Your Child Struggles by David Cook. And it had a checklist in it of things to ask the child. And I was thinking about it in relationship to children that I was experiencing at school when I was substitute teaching. But I practiced.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:14:29\u8211\'9600:14:29]\line Oh, okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:14:29\u8211\'9600:14:50]\line I decided to practice the questions on my daughter. And so I said to her, do the words ever do this when you're reading? And, you know, they split apart. And she said yes. And I thought, oh, that's not good. I had no idea that she was seeing double.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:14:50\u8211\'9600:14:52]\line And how old was she at this point? Remind me.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:14:52\u8211\'9600:14:54]\line She was 9.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:14:54\u8211\'9600:14:55]\line Okay. So about\u8212\'97 okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:14:55\u8211\'9600:15:37]\line Yeah. Yeah. So very starting to be very aware of that and potentially have problems later on, you know. Because reading just\u8212\'97 the words just keep getting smaller, right? And more difficult. So I said, well, do you ever close an eye when you're reading? That was also on the checklist. And she said, oh yeah, all the time. When I'm reading in bed, I lay with my eye on the pillow so that I'm reading just with the one eye. And she said, and then I turn over when I turn the page and do it with the other eye. So that was helping avoid double vision, right? And I had\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:15:37\u8211\'9600:15:45]\line Yeah, like she kind of figured it out. Like she had her own solution. I mean, it was a coping mechanism, basically.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:15:45\u8211\'9600:16:43]\line Exactly. Yes. And I don't know if she did any of that at school. Sometimes children will, you know, they'll sit with their hand up like this, you know, cover an eye and just make other compensatory items that will help them to not have that problem. So she was doing all of those things.\line I had no idea. And I thought I was a pretty aware mom. She was trying to have kids. I'm sure you were. Yeah.\line Right. Right. I was busy, but I kind of was beating myself up a little bit about it. So I took her into my vision therapy doctor, and he got her in vision therapy. It took about 9 months of therapy for her, and she was able to gain 3D. So it's a pretty easy process.\line It is something for a lot of people that you kind of have to keep doing a little bit of to keep the skill.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:16:43\u8211\'9600:16:45]\line Kind of like exercise in a way.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:16:45\u8211\'9600:17:02]\line A little bit, yeah. So I think she might have lost a little ground. We've talked about that over the years. She's been on my podcast too. And told her story. So she recognizes that there might be some things she could do to kind of strengthen her ability still. And in the meantime, my doctor\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:17:02\u8211\'9600:17:05]\line It takes time and effort to do that. It does.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:17:05\u8211\'9600:17:25]\line Yeah, it does. And for some people, it takes way longer, you know, and there are cases that take less time. But I think 9 months is a fairly standard or comfortable amount of time that it will take for people, if they're\u8212\'97 for kids, you know, kids are much more malleable than adults are. So\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:17:25\u8211\'9600:17:26]\line Oh, yeah, absolutely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:17:26\u8211\'9600:17:58]\line I went back in at the end of that process. My doctor had done some training in some other kinds of therapy. I went in, I tried those, and still wasn't getting the results I wanted. At this point, I'm like 80 sessions into vision therapy. And once again, he said, you probably need to look at surgery. So he referred me to a doctor that he's worked with. I went in, I had the strabismus surgery.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:17:59\u8211\'9600:17:59]\line Okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:17:59\u8211\'9600:18:08]\line You know, don't know what that looks like. It's, you know, you go in, they cut all the muscles and they move them so that your eyes are lined up instead of crossed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:18:08\u8211\'9600:18:29]\line Wow. I mean, that's a big, big step. I could see why you, you know, you would want to avoid it if at all possible. I think anytime For most of us, right? You talk about our eyes or eye surgery, it's just, it's different. It hits different than just saying, oh, you know, you, we got to do some elbow surgery, for example, or something like that.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:18:29\u8211\'9600:18:35]\line Well, I mean, when you're cutting a muscle, I think you tend to hesitate before you're\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:18:35\u8211\'9600:18:46]\line It's your eyes. It's your eyes. All right. Like, that's very, very personal to all of us. So, but it sounds like it was It sounds like obviously it was a success.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:18:46\u8211\'9600:19:09]\line Yeah, it was amazing. I had a really easy time with the surgery. I took like one pain med. I decided the pain meds weren't really helping me, not doing good things to my body. I said, not doing that. And so I'm really into natural remedies. So I took this homeopathic remedy called Arnica.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:19:10\u8211\'9600:19:11]\line Oh, okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:19:11\u8211\'9600:19:22]\line Instead of any of the other drugs they had given me. And I went back for my checkup a week later. And my eye doctor said, I can't believe how fast you've recovered from this surgery.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:19:22\u8211\'9600:19:23]\line Wow.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:19:23\u8211\'9600:19:48]\line I said, great, thank you. And that week, I also went back into vision therapy. And they don't necessarily recommend that you do that. You know, a lot of times doctors will say, oh, you should, Recover first or whatever. I mean, I was recovered, but not everybody will go back in that quickly. And as soon as I went back in, I could do everything that I hadn't been able to do before.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:19:48\u8211\'9600:19:52]\line Wow. Wow. That must have been amazing.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:19:52\u8211\'9600:20:05]\line It was. Yeah. And I gained, you know, pretty good depth perception, especially close up. My depth perception is in normal range. Further out, it's not quite as good. So I'm still working on that.}
