 [00:24:56\u8211\'9600:24:56]\line Okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:24:56\u8211\'9600:25:30]\line We're, we're training the brain to see correctly because the eyes themselves are just an organ, right? They\u8212\'97 the muscles are not going to do anything you don't tell them to do. So if the brain isn't telling the eyes what to do, you're not going to see properly regardless. You know, it really\u8212\'97 vision really is just in the brain. And we don't think of it that way. We think our eyes are seeing, you know, but I mean, our arm's not going to move if our brain doesn't tell it to. So why do we think our eyes know what to do if our brain doesn't tell them what to do?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:25:30\u8211\'9600:26:03]\line Why do we think that, Denise? That's a good question. I mean, because it's true. That's absolutely the perception. You don't think of it as a muscle. You don't think of it as something that your brain has to control, I guess, unless you're really in a situation when you\u8212\'97 that kind of focus is required. Um, anything from like looking through a microscope or binoculars or, you know, whatever, where you're like, oh, you know, you're actually focused on the task at hand. I guess you just take it for granted. I mean\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:26:03\u8211\'9600:26:08]\line We all take it for granted all the time. And do you\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:26:08\u8211\'9600:26:29]\line Yeah, yeah, go ahead. Kind of like walking. Again, you, you take advantage\u8212\'97 you, you take it for granted if you're able to walk, right? If you've gone through that progression, you know, that's all you know. You, you learn to crawl, you learn to walk. You want to go from point A to point B, you walk there. You don't think about your brain's telling your legs to move.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:26:29\u8211\'9600:26:31]\line Exactly.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:26:32\u8211\'9600:26:34]\line I guess it's the same for vision.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:26:34\u8211\'9600:26:56]\line And if our eye muscles aren't working properly, it's no different than any other muscle in our body, you know, and we do exercise to strengthen those muscles or to relax those muscles, right? And in the case of our eyes, we really need to relax the muscles in order for them to see properly. And we never think of it that way either, you know.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:26:57\u8211\'9600:27:22]\line No, not at all. I mean, you're starting to see some awareness in terms of eyes. I'm thinking about like with eye fatigue now with all the screen time, you know, things kind of related to that. Hey, you need to give your eyes a break. You know, you don't want to be staring at a screen for hours on end and, and all that. But I still feel like it's fairly shallow in terms of the approach that we take.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
