 [00:27:22\u8211\'9600:27:25]\line I agree. Absolutely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:27:27\u8211\'9600:27:43]\line Yep. Um, yeah, I was thinking also with, especially with kids and screen time, and, you know, this all overlaps, but could some, you know, could these problems sometimes look like ADHD or learning disabilities or sensory issues?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:27:43\u8211\'9600:28:10]\line Absolutely. Yeah. And the fact that we see it in this population should point that out a little bit. You know, if the same kids that are struggling are the ones who have a vision problem, then, you know, which came first? And what's the best way to deal with it, right? And, you know, I have another favorite book that I wanted to share.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:28:10\u8211\'9600:28:11]\line Yeah, please.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:28:11\u8211\'9600:28:38]\line There's, well, there's a couple that were written by Robin and Jillian Benoit. One of them's called Jillian's Story. And then I have this one, Dear Jillian. And they talk in this book about\u8212\'97 well, in the first one, she tells Jillian's story. And Jillian had amblyopia. She had passed every eye exam. And the way she passed it\u8212\'97 and I don't know if you know what amblyopia is.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:28:38\u8211\'9600:28:39]\line I do not.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:28:39\u8211\'9600:28:51]\line Okay, well, it's a type of strabismus. Amblyopia, you have lower acuity in one eye. So if you can't see very well out of one eye, you're just going to use the other eye.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:28:51\u8211\'9600:28:51]\line Okay.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:28:51\u8211\'9600:29:33]\line And that eye just kind of shuts off. And sometimes if that happens for a long period of time, the person really goes blind in that eye. And it just kind of becomes\u8212\'97 they treat it as a permanent kind of problem. I don't agree that any of that's permanent, but There's different perceptions on that. Anyway, Jillian had, um, pretty significant amblyopia, but she'd passed every test when they've done the eye exam at the school because she thought it was like a memorization test.\line And so she would listen to the kids in front of her, and she wanted to get the treat, right? And so she would just rattle off whatever they said, even though she couldn't see it at all.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:29:33\u8211\'9600:29:40]\line Wow. That's\u8212\'97 I mean, it's ingenious, but Not helpful in terms of\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:29:40\u8211\'9600:30:03]\line Exactly. Yeah. And so when she finally got into vision therapy, then, you know, she was able to overcome that and gain 3D vision and then tell her story, you know. And then all these people started writing to her saying, hey, let me tell you my story. And that's what went into the second book, right? And she did talk to someone that was autistic.}
