David Kaufer}{
 [00:49:10\u8211\'9600:49:52]\line Yeah, and so we're going to start off, and for each of these, just give you fair warning, we do have little jingles that will\u8212\'97 that Dave, producer Dave, will play. And then we'll get\u8212\'97 we'll start off with the tip of the week. It won't necessarily be Autism Tip of the Week, but it'll be Denise's Tip of the Week. Hey parents, gather around, it's time to speak. We're here with your tip of the week, strategies and wisdom just for you.\line Autism parents, we know what you go through. All right, it's time for our tip of the week, and as I mentioned earlier, I know that Denise, you brought one for us. What do you have?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:49:53\u8211\'9600:50:10]\line Well, we've kind of talked about it a little bit already, but I'm just pointing to the fact that a child may be able to see clearly and still have difficulty using their 2 eyes together. And a regular vision screening, even at a doctor's office, may not tell the whole story.}
