Denise Allen}{
 [00:51:06\u8211\'9600:51:17]\line Get QuickTime ready, and here we go. This is Autism Fact or Fiction. We're breaking down what's real, what's rumor, and what might surprise you. Let's go.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:51:17\u8211\'9600:51:32]\line All right, so this is again where I like to introduce potential stereotypes or myths or, you know, things that may misperceive\u8212\'97 misperceptions that may be out there. But, um, Denise, what do you have for fact or fiction?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:51:32\u8211\'9600:51:48]\line Well, again, we've talked about a lot of this, so I'm kind of feeling like maybe this is just a review. Uh, the fact or fiction that I chose was, uh, 20/20 means that your vision is fine.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:51:50\u8211\'9600:52:07]\line Right. I think that's a big one, though. I think that bears repeating because I think that's such a\u8212\'97 that I think that's just presumed to be fact. I think that's just so ingrained in us that that's the goal. It's just all about 20/20 vision that you don't even think about that.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:52:07\u8211\'9600:52:18]\line Right. And because my glasses corrected my vision so that it was 20/20, I must be fine, right? Yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:52:19\u8211\'9600:52:29]\line Yeah. And I guess kind of related to that would be, you know, I jotted down, you know, like my child passed their vision screening, you know, at school. So everything's fine.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:52:29\u8211\'9600:52:30]\line Yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:52:30\u8211\'9600:52:32]\line Not true.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:52:32\u8211\'9600:52:35]\line And being told that you're fine for years and years and years.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:52:35\u8211\'9600:52:37]\line Oh, yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:52:37\u8211\'9600:52:39]\line And knowing that you're not really.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:52:41\u8211\'9600:52:51]\line I mean, there's, there's a little bit of trauma that goes with that, right? I mean, kind of, isn't it a little bit of being like gaslit for so many years? Like, you're like, I know this isn't true, but I can't prove it.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:52:51\u8211\'9600:52:55]\line Yes. And I've heard it from many of my guests as well.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:52:55\u8211\'9600:53:00]\line That they knew, that they knew something was wrong, but\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:53:00\u8211\'9600:53:23]\line Yeah. And, and one in particular had the cerebismus surgery. And went back to her surgeon and said, you know, I'm really struggling. She had a complete breakdown of her visual system after her surgery. You know, you move the eyes around, she's used to compensating a certain way, and her eyes had no idea what to do at that point. And this was\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:53:23\u8211\'9600:53:23]\line Wow.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:53:23\u8211\'9600:53:33]\line A while after the surgery that she had this complete breakdown, and they treated her like she was crazy, like she should just\u8212\'97 but they literally said, It's all in your head.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Plot/Intro}{
 [00:53:36\u8211\'9600:53:36]\line Unbelievable.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:53:37\u8211\'9600:53:43]\line It was all in her head because it was her brain not knowing how to tell her eyes how to work together.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:53:43\u8211\'9600:54:17]\line Right, right, right. Now I go back to the, the point you made right off the bat, Denise, in terms of how our eyes are muscles. And if you're going to have surgery on a muscle, it's just like anything else. Like, I can't imagine someone who goes through, say, you know, again, sports-related, that people relate, you know, can go through ACL surgery and just like, you just have surgery and then say, okay, you're good to go without PT, right? Without any type of follow-up. I mean, it sounds like that's kind of the expectation with, with eye, the eye surgery.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:54:17\u8211\'9600:54:29]\line It is. Yeah. And that's actually one of my favorite analogies. You would never have surgery on any other part of your body and not have physical therapy before surgery or after surgery or both.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:54:30\u8211\'9600:54:30]\line Right.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:54:30\u8211\'9600:54:35]\line Right. And yet that's what we are doing all the time with vision, with our eyes, with our eye surgery.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:54:35\u8211\'9600:54:57]\line That's crazy. Sorry, that really is crazy. I mean, that's just, um, I guess it just seems\u8212\'97 yeah, it seems like there's\u8212\'97 we need to progress the view there, and as we have in so many other areas of medicine and healthcare. I'll put it that way. Saying it's just crazy isn't very productive.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:54:58\u8211\'9600:55:07]\line Well, it's, it's not, but the awareness is what we're trying to do so that people will know that there needs to be a change. You know, we, we have to demand it of the doctors.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:55:07\u8211\'9600:55:50]\line Right. Yeah. And that's, yeah, and that's kind of like a whole nother conversation, right, Denise, is changing our mindset, um, as patients in general, as advocates for our kids, you know, dealing with doctors, um, Trusting them as experts, which they are. They're trained. They're, you know, they have a lot of education and training, which deserves respect.\line But that doesn't mean they're all-knowing, all-knowing, and they, and they don't know our bodies. I mean, they can't. At best, a lot of what they're doing is still kind of making educated guesses about the approach, which, you know, that's just the way it works.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:55:51\u8211\'9600:56:00]\line But\u8212\'97 And it's true in the vision therapy room, too. They have to figure out where the missing piece is, you know?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Plot/Intro}{
 [00:56:00\u8211\'9600:56:00]\line Mm-hmm.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:56:00\u8211\'9600:56:01]\line Right.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:56:01\u8211\'9600:56:26]\line And you can talk about vision therapy with relation to traumatic brain injury and everything, too. And, you know, I've had many of my guests that work with that population say, if you've treated one person with a traumatic brain injury, you've treated one person with a traumatic brain injury, you know? So there's just a lot of things going on with that, you know? And I think some of the autistic population falls into that traumatic brain injury category too, right?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:56:27\u8211\'9600:56:27]\line Yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [00:56:27\u8211\'9600:56:32]\line And so it's just they're practicing medicine, you know, they're, they're trying to figure it out.}
