David Kaufer}{
 [01:01:29\u8211\'9601:01:39]\line All right, so like I said, what do you have for us, Denise, to give, give our listeners, parents out there, a little bit of hope?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [01:01:39\u8211\'9601:02:04]\line Well, I think that my story is my biggest gift, right? Because neuroplasticity is a real thing. You know, you don't have to say, oh, this is just the way it is. And I mean, I've heard it so many times. People will say, I have permanent double vision. I will never see in 3D.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [01:02:04\u8211\'9601:02:05]\line Mm.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [01:02:05\u8211\'9601:02:56]\line Happens all the time, you know. And when I went into my surgeon for my first visit with him and I told him that my goal was to see in 3D, he didn't take that super well, really. You know, he, he actually told me that he wanted me to come back in and do some more testing because they were getting some new machine in there that was going to be able to gauge whether I'd be successful, that kind of thing. And I already knew I was going to be successful.\line But he didn't, you know, and so I waited and I went back in and I did their other testing and stuff and found out that he actually, and I'm, it probably shouldn't share, but I knew he, that he thought that I was being unrealistic.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [01:02:56\u8211\'9601:03:05]\line Right. Sure. He's being overly, overly cautious or overly skeptical or choose your, choose your word. Right.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [01:03:05\u8211\'9601:03:13]\line I mean, right. Right. But I mean, neuroplasticity says our brains can change, right? The way we see\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [01:03:13\u8211\'9601:03:14]\line 100%.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Denise Allen}{
 [01:03:14\u8211\'9601:03:24]\line The way we see can change. The way we do things can change. Our bodies can improve in many different ways, right? We see that all the time at every age.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
